Render environment: OpenSCAD 2025.06.12.ai25773 (default CGAL engine), binary
STL; BOSL2 https://github.com/BelfrySCAD/BOSL2 commit
b86a7584db6d324eb856c2d19d041f94435e6c32 checked out at $BOSL2_PARENT/BOSL2.
Each mesh renders the UNMODIFIED source with -D overrides only, from the
staged directory:

    OPENSCADPATH=$BOSL2_PARENT openscad --export-format=binstl -o OUT.stl FILE.scad [-D ...]

Mayor renders (pre-flight, city assets/incoming/underware-ref/, copied
byte-for-byte; the mayor's baseline hashes):
  mesh/i-1x5-h22.stl  monokini_I_channel.scad, defaults (1 x 5 units, height 22).
      Byte-identical under BOSL2 456fcd8 (the repo pin) and b86a7584.
  mesh/l.stl          monokini_L_channel.scad, defaults.
  mesh/t.stl          monokini_T_channel.scad, defaults.
  mesh/x.stl          monokini_X_channel.scad, defaults.
  L and T are BOSL2-pin-sensitive (L: 8.67 cm3 / 15392 facets at b86a7584 vs
  9.00 cm3 / 14672 at 456fcd8; T facet counts differ by 4); X is
  facet-identical but byte-different. Never re-render these at the repo pin
  to "refresh" them. A worker re-render of L at b86a7584 reproduces 15392
  facets / 8669.58 mm3 with a different byte order (CGAL facet order), so the
  committed bytes are the mayor's.

